{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_slm6b3zcempo34cp4kfsjq3ox33wzgjs6y2gddoynolg2hlpznua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 12 tests pass (within the 60-second timeout, ~8 seconds each run). The build also succeeded without errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the C `simple_sparsehash` library to safe, idiomatic Rust without using `unsafe` or FFI. Key implementation choices:\n\n**Sparse Array (`SparseArrayGroup`)** — Rather than mimicking C's fixed-size slot layout (`elem_size + sizeof(size_t)` per occupied slot), I used a variable-sized layout in `Vec<u8>`:\n- Each entry is stored as `[vlen: u64 LE][value bytes]`\n- `position_to_offset` uses `u32::count_ones()` for popcount\n- Insertion uses `Vec::splice`/`drain` to grow or shrink slots in place\n\n**Sparse Dictionary** — Buckets are serialized into the underlying sparse array as `[klen][vlen][hash][key bytes][value bytes]`:\n- `hash_fnv1a` mirrors the C FNV-1a hash exactly (with `wrapping_mul` to handle u64 overflow)\n- Quadratic probing uses `(hash + n*n) & (max - 1)`\n- Resize triggers at `bucket_count * 100 >= bucket_max * RESIZE_PERCENT`, then rebuilds via `rehash_and_grow`\n\n**Free functions** — Just drop the `Box`, since Rust handles deallocation.\n\nAll 12 tests pass, including the million-iteration `test_dict_lots_of_set`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1533,"cache_read_input_tokens":49150,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1533,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ff49af5b-0797-4775-83e8-4a8654f802da","uuid":"f2490721-3ec2-4d8c-845d-084ce8bc64a3"}
